{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"91570","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/91570","key":"MC-265060","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"26/Aug/23 12:03 PM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"Thebug\"></a>The bug</h3>\n\n<p>When you try to add more than 6 patterns to a banner in a loom you don't get any error or message.</p>\n\n<p>However, the Minecraft code can show an icon in the loom GUI when you add a banner with 6 or more patterns (for example, the Ominous banner).</p>\n\n<p>The problem is that the gui/container/loom.png file does not have the appropiate sprite to show this error.</p>\n\n<p>This bug exists also in the new 1.20.2 snapshots, because there is not an error sprite in gui/sprites/container/loom directory.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce\"></a>How to reproduce</h3>\n\n<p>Open the Loom GUI and put the Ominous banner in the first slot (or any banner with 6 patterns).</p>\n<h3><a name=\"Actualbehavior\"></a>Actual behavior</h3>\n\n<p>The GUI does not show any error, but you cannot add more patterns to that banner. See picture \"1 without pack error not visible.png\"</p>\n<h3><a name=\"Expectedbehavior\"></a>Expected behavior</h3>\n\n<p>You should see something like a red X because you cannot add more patterns to than banner. See picture \"3 with pack error &nbsp;visible (red X).png\"</p>\n<h3><a name=\"Correctedfile\"></a>Corrected file</h3>\n\n<p>I have attached a very simple resource pack with only a modified gui/container/loom.png file with an added sprite (Loom Error Demo.zip). I have also attached the file here directly.</p>\n\n<p>When you use this resource pack and repeat the steps, then you get a red X in the final slot if the banner already has 6 or more patterns.</p>\n\n<p>Regretly, this correction does not work in the 1.20.2 snapshots.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"Disclaimer\"></a>Disclaimer</h3>\n\n<p>I think this is a bug and not a change request because the code for using this sprite is already in Minecraft 1.20.1 (and earlier). It is just that the sprite is missing in the texture file.</p>\n\n<p>I don't know if the code has changed for 1.20.2.</p>\n\n<p>Sorry, I am not an English speaker. So, please rewrite this description if you think it is necessary for better understanding.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"27/Aug/23 12:42 AM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/119271","id":"119271","filename":"1 without pack error not visible.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"stargazer","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Los_Angeles","accountType":"customer"},"created":"26/Aug/23 11:50 AM","size":"56 kB","mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/119271","thumbnail":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/thumbnail/119271"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/119272","id":"119272","filename":"2 without pack correct banner.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us